;; #336 L3 METTA ENCODING (reconstructed 2026-10-22 under #513) Attention Sinks × RLCT. TYPE DECLS: (: head Concept) (: parameter Concept) (: functional Concept) (: subposterior Concept) (: rlct Concept) (: stratum Concept) (: step Concept) (: length Concept) (: score Concept) (: context Concept). D1: head h has parameter subset within Theta; context tokens (k_j, v_jeach j. D2: (-> functional head) sink functional S_h = attention mass on first r sink positions; softmax mass conservation sum_j a_j = 1 definable via exp inner products, affine projection, rational sum-to-one. D3: (-> subposterior functional) Theta_sink = fiber of w where S_h >= 1 - epsilon on near-universal sink head set under mismatch contexts; posterior restricted to it. D4: (-> rlct subposterior) lambda_sink = local RLCT of sink-restricted fiber, finite by resolution of singularities. D5: stratum selector: sink magnitude s = S_h(w) or sink token count r indexes strata; Theta = disjoint union Theta_sink and complement Theta_nonsink. D6: StreamingLLM cache keeps sink positions fixed, selecting the sink stratum for streaming. D7: (-> step score) training step t to lambda_sink(t); streaming critical length L* beyond which non-sink heads need sink stratum to satisfy mass conservation; sink emergence during training at step t*. C1 PROVEN stv 1.0 0.95: (Implication (Inheritance S_h R_an-definable) (Inheritance (fiber-over w) FiniteRLCT)) — finite composition of analytic maps; R_an closed under composition; resolution of singularities; same definability class as #303/#508/#512 C1. C2 CONJECTURAL stv 0.6 0.8: (Implication (Inheritance Theta_sink low-rlct-stratum) (less lambda_sink lambda_full)) — gap: posterior concentration on sink fiber unproven. C3 CONJECTURAL stv 0.5 0.75: (Implication (greater s effective-rlct-decreases) per-head SGLD measurable) — gap: head-restricted SGLD estimator unestablished (P1). C4 CONJECTURAL stv 0.5 0.7: (Implication (greater L L*) (collapse-without-sink-stratum)) — cache eviction of sinks = crossing strata, links #229; gap: no bound on L*. C5 CONJECTURAL stv 0.5 0.7: (Inheritance mass-conservation-singularity generic-codim0) — almost all trained models develop sinks; gap: transversality unproven, sink vs retrieval-head fiber interplay open (#512 P6). CAVEATS: (1) C2-C5 rest on posterior concentration assumption; (2) head-restricted RLCT estimator not established; (3) L* and t* unquantified; (4) refined-LLC head differentiation adjacent non-SLT baseline; (5) falsified if lambda_sink >= lambda_full in trained models per P6. OPEN PROBLEMS: P1 head-wise SGLD estimator; P2 sink heads vs retrieval heads same stratum or distinct fibers (#512 P6); P3 sink token count r dependence on positional encoding; P4 KV-cache eviction as stratum crossing (#229); P5 pretraining vs streaming emergence of sinks; P6 falsification condition. CROSS-REFS: #229 #292 #302 #396 #512 #8 #16 #57 #73 #100. NEXT: L4 summary + L5 catalog append.